card.statement:
Fix $r\in\Z_{>0}$ and let $s\in\iv{1}{r}$. Let $\si\in S_r$ be the permutation which gives rise to the leading term of $d_{rs}$. That is,

\begin{equation}
\lt(d_{rs}) = \la t_{\si(1)1}^{(k_1)}t_{\si(2)2}^{(k_2)}\cdots t_{\si(r)r}^{(k_r)}
\end{equation}

for some nonzero $\la\in\C$ and some $k\in\{0,1\}^r$ with $\sum_i k_i=s$. Then

\begin{equation}
\height(\si) = 2s(r-s).
\end{equation}
